The provided class implements an asynchronous, time‑based reactive operator that relies on external `Scheduler` implementations and real‑time delays. JMH is designed for deterministic, in‑process microbenchmarks; measuring throughput of a component that schedules work on separate threads and depends on wall‑clock timing would yield unreliable results and require extensive harness code to control time and backpressure. Consequently, a JMH benchmark is not appropriate for this source.